// CONTRACT (must-error): the `unknown type` diagnostic ends by naming the spelling the author
// almost certainly wanted, from TWO sources, and the refusal itself is unchanged (D1590).
//
// The first line is glean's report VL-039 verbatim — `{[i32]: bool}`, the map annotation a
// reader coming from any other language writes first. The message was correct and pointed at
// the right span; it just stopped one word short of ending the session.
//
//   1 A SPELLING MAP for newcomers, exact and case-folded: `bool`/`int`/`float`/`str` and
//     friends name a VL primitive without becoming one. None of them is accepted as a type.
//   2 An EDIT DISTANCE over the names in scope — the built-ins plus every declared
//     `type`/struct/union — budgeted by length (1 up to 4 characters, 2 up to 8, 3 beyond).
//
// The suffix is a SUFFIX: `unknown type 'bool' within '{[i32]:bool}'` is the prefix every
// existing consumer matches on, and it is byte-identical to what this diagnostic said before.
// `unknown-type-no-near-name.vl` is the negative control — a name with nothing near it keeps
